                  "markdown":  "---\nname: dependency-advisory-graph\ndescription: Match dependency manifests to advisory evidence with exact package and version checks.\nsource:\n  type: cli-tool\n  command: node\n  args:\n    - run.mjs\nrunx:\n  category: security\n---\n\n# Dependency Advisory Graph\n\nProduce a reviewer-safe advisory packet for one dependency manifest.\n\nThis skill is intentionally conservative. It only reports a finding when the\npackage name, ecosystem, and installed version exactly match supplied advisory\nevidence. Package-name-only matches are treated as insufficient evidence.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Read one manifest and one advisory list.\n2. Normalize dependency names, ecosystems, and versions.\n3. Match only exact installed versions against advisory `affected_versions`.\n4. Emit a clean or unknown result when no exact version match exists.\n5. Preserve the advisory source URL, retrieved timestamp, and optional graph\n   receipt so a reviewer can trace the evidence.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `manifest`: dependency manifest with `ecosystem` and `dependencies`.\n- `advisories`: advisory records with package, affected versions, and source.\n- `graph_receipt`: optional receipt ref from an upstream research graph.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `package`, `installed_version`, `advisory_id`, `evidence_url`.\n- `advisory_source`, `retrieved_at`, `severity`, `fix_version`.\n- `confidence`, `graph_receipt`, `findings`, and `evidence`.\n\n",
                  "profile_document":  "skill: dependency-advisory-graph\nversion: \"0.1.0\"\n\ncatalog:\n  kind: skill\n  audience: public\n  visibility: public\n  role: canonical\n\nharness:\n  cases:\n    - name: dependency-advisory-exact-match\n      runner: graph\n      inputs:\n        manifest:\n          ecosystem: npm\n          dependencies:\n            lodash: 4.17.20\n            undici: 6.19.8\n        advisories:\n          - package: lodash\n            ecosystem: npm\n            affected_versions:\n              - 4.17.20\n            advisory_id: GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm\n            evidence_url: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm\n            advisory_source: GitHub Advisory Database\n            retrieved_at: \"2026-06-21T00:00:00Z\"\n            severity: high\n            fix_version: 4.17.21\n        graph_receipt: runx:receipt:graph-demo-001\n      expect:\n        status: sealed\n        receipt:\n          schema: runx.receipt.v1\n    - name: dependency-advisory-clean-manifest\n      runner: graph\n      inputs:\n        manifest:\n          ecosystem: npm\n          dependencies:\n            lodash: 4.17.21\n        advisories:\n          - package: lodash\n            ecosystem: npm\n            affected_versions:\n              - 4.17.20\n            advisory_id: GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm\n            evidence_url: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm\n            advisory_source: GitHub Advisory Database\n            retrieved_at: \"2026-06-21T00:00:00Z\"\n            severity: high\n            fix_version: 4.17.21\n      expect:\n        status: sealed\n        receipt:\n          schema: runx.receipt.v1\n\nrunners:\n  graph:\n    default: true\n    type: cli-tool\n    command: node\n    args:\n      - run.mjs\n    outputs:\n      status: string\n      package: string\n      installed_version: string\n      advisory_id: string\n      evidence_url: string\n      advisory_source: string\n      retrieved_at: string\n      severity: string\n      fix_version: string\n      confidence: string\n      graph_receipt: string\n      evidence: object\n      findings: object\n    artifacts:\n      wrap_as: dependency_advisory_graph_packet\n      packet: runx.security.dependency_advisory_graph.v1\n    inputs:\n      manifest:\n        type: json\n        required: true\n        description: Dependency manifest with ecosystem and dependencies.\n      advisories:\n        type: json\n        required: true\n        description: Advisory records with exact affected versions and evidence URLs.\n      graph_receipt:\n        type: string\n        required: false\n        description: Receipt ref from an upstream vulnerability or research graph.\n\n",
